WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.921
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.811 --> 00:00:07.936
Looking to accelerate
your open-source data

00:00:07.936 --> 00:00:09.691
and analytics processing?

00:00:09.691 --> 00:00:13.490
Give me one minute
and I'll show you how with <i>Cloud Dataproc</i>.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.351
<i>Dataproc</i> is a managed service
for any OSS jobs

00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:20.465
that support big data processing
including ETL and machine learning.

00:00:20.465 --> 00:00:24.878
It provides out-of-the-box support
for the most popular open-source software.

00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:27.838
You can use <i>Dataproc</i>
to move your on premise OSS clusters

00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:28.950
to the cloud,

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.861
to maximize efficiency and enable scale.

00:00:31.861 --> 00:00:34.592
Or, use it with <i>Cloud AI Notebook</i>
or <i>BigQuery</i>

00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:37.414
to build an end-to-end
data science environment.

00:00:37.414 --> 00:00:41.079
With <i>Dataproc</i>, you can spin up
an IT governed, auto-scaling cluster

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:43.179
in just 90 seconds.

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:45.812
It manages the cluster creation,
monitoring,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.352
and job orchestration for you.

00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:52.149
Start by creating a cluster
through the web UI, Cloud SDK,

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:55.215
REST APIs, or with SSH access.

00:00:55.215 --> 00:00:57.766
Once your cluster's provisioned,
you can submit jobs

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:00.170
in your opensource framework of choice.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.216
Scale your cluster up or down at any time
even when jobs are running

00:01:04.216 --> 00:01:07.222
and you'll pay only for what you use
down to the second.

00:01:07.222 --> 00:01:09.449
Next time you're looking
to simplify your data

00:01:09.449 --> 00:01:10.782
and analytics processing,

00:01:10.782 --> 00:01:12.842
take a minute to look at <i>Dataproc</i>.

00:01:12.842 --> 00:01:16.992
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/dataproc.

